<%# src/views/partials/task-earn-pitch.ejs
    Issue #926 review fix (MAJOR M4): the SINGLE place that renders the guest
    task list's earn-pitch line — "Best photos earn [badge name] + bonus
    points" — as three spans (a fixed lead, the one variable-width name, a
    fixed tail) laid out as a nowrap line where ONLY the name may shrink and
    ellipsize (see .task-earnable-copy's own comment, src/public/css/
    theme.css, for the sizing math). Before this partial existed,
    src/views/partials/task-todo-row.ejs (the to-do row) and the done-rows
    loop in src/views/tasks.ejs each carried their own copy of this identical
    three-span markup — two owners of one sentence, with nothing stopping a
    wording tweak or a class rename made in one copy from silently not
    reaching the other. Every guest-list call site includes this partial
    instead now, the same "one owner, why" shape badge-art.ejs's own header
    comment already sets for how a badge's ART renders — this partial is that
    same discipline applied to the WORDS beside it.

    Local:
      badge (required) - { name, ... } (task-badges.toTaskBadgeView's shape).
        Only .name is read here; the badge's ART is a separate concern (see
        badge-art.ejs), rendered independently by each call site (a large
        leading .task-badge-lead on a to-do row, the guest's own photo
        thumbnail on a done row) — this partial owns the WORDS only, never
        the art.
%>
<span class="task-earnable-copy"
  ><span class="task-earnable-lead">Best photos earn</span
  ><span class="task-earnable-name"><%= badge.name %></span
  ><span class="task-earnable-tail">+ bonus points</span
></span>
